WEBVTT

00:00:25.636 --> 00:00:29.630
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:00:29.706 --> 00:00:33.472
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:13.370
Blade... It's seems like ages
since we were last here.

00:02:13.443 --> 00:02:16.310
It may feel like ages,
but it was only three years ago.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.180
Still, the mood of the city
definitely seems to have changed.

00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:23.049
There are a lot
more people here now.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.523
A lot of refugees must have come
here to escape the chaos of war.

00:02:27.591 --> 00:02:29.889
Everyone wants peace...

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.930
...but the only place to
find it on Lodoss now...

00:02:32.996 --> 00:02:36.193
...is in Flaim and
the free city of Raiden.

00:02:36.266 --> 00:02:38.428
Hey, look over there.

00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:40.129
Why, you...!

00:02:41.605 --> 00:02:42.970
A fight?

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.132
Looks that way.

00:02:44.207 --> 00:02:44.969
Let's check it out!

00:02:45.042 --> 00:02:47.841
But, Parn! We have to get to
King Kashue as soon as we--

00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:54.342
Oh, this ALWAYS happens!

00:02:59.656 --> 00:03:00.885
Are you all right, Dear?!

00:03:00.957 --> 00:03:02.982
Daddy!

00:03:03.093 --> 00:03:05.152
We've had enough of you people!

00:03:05.228 --> 00:03:09.028
Especially since you're here only
on the good graces of King Kashue!

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:12.933
But you act like thieves!
You people are scum!

00:03:14.971 --> 00:03:16.666
Look carefully, you people!

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.801
Under King Kashue's rule, Flaim
considers theft to be a serious crime!

00:03:30.454 --> 00:03:32.479
What?!

00:03:38.762 --> 00:03:41.390
Wh- Who are you?!

00:03:42.399 --> 00:03:44.265
That should be my line!

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:47.395
From where I'm standing,
you're attacking an unarmed man!

00:03:48.805 --> 00:03:49.567
Are you all right?

00:03:49.639 --> 00:03:52.939
He's a thief! He stole this!

00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:55.376
Then shouldn't you
return it to its owner?

00:03:55.445 --> 00:03:58.506
King Kashue would never
permit what you're doing!

00:03:58.582 --> 00:04:01.574
Shut up! This isn't any of your
business, so stay out of it!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.813
Don't be foolish. You're just
going to get yourselves hurt.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.449
Parn!

00:04:08.525 --> 00:04:10.550
| know! I'll go easy on them.

00:04:23.607 --> 00:04:26.076
All right, who'll be next?

00:04:26.143 --> 00:04:28.840
Hold it! Hold it!

00:04:33.683 --> 00:04:38.780
Who are you people, who help thieves
and hurt our city's citizens?!

00:04:38.855 --> 00:04:41.222
W- Wait a minute,
just hear me out--

00:04:41.291 --> 00:04:44.226
Silence!
You'd better come along quietly.

00:04:44.294 --> 00:04:46.956
If you don't, I'll cut you down
right here without any mercy!

00:04:47.664 --> 00:04:51.225
| guess there's no
reasoning with you, huh?

00:04:51.301 --> 00:04:54.464
Parn, no!
You mustn't fight them!

00:04:54.538 --> 00:04:56.438
D- Did he say Parn?!

00:04:56.506 --> 00:04:59.567
Can it be...?! Wait!
Sheathe your swords, all of you!

00:05:01.178 --> 00:05:05.877
By any chance, are you Sir Parn, the
knight who saved Flaim from peril?

00:05:05.949 --> 00:05:08.043
Well, I AM Parn, yes.

00:05:08.118 --> 00:05:10.951
Although saying I saved Flaim
is exaggerating things.

00:05:11.021 --> 00:05:15.049
F- Forgive me, sir! We had no
idea you were coming to Flaim!

00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:18.686
No, please. I'm sorry for making
this disturbance even worse.

00:05:18.762 --> 00:05:21.629
However, I saw these
militia men ganging up...

00:05:21.698 --> 00:05:24.633
...on that refugee and
trying to beat him.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.398
So, that's the reason.
Now I understand.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.303
There's a serious
food shortage here in Flaim...

00:05:30.373 --> 00:05:33.900
...because we've had so many
refugees come here at once.

00:05:33.977 --> 00:05:35.945
People are going hungry?

00:05:36.012 --> 00:05:38.071
Yes, and because of it, there's
a lot of anger building up...

00:05:38.148 --> 00:05:40.276
...among the citizenry
against the refugees.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:43.547
Disturbances like this
are becoming a daily occurrence.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.419
Are you headed
for Akroyd, Sir Parn?

00:05:46.489 --> 00:05:48.924
Well, yes. I am.

00:05:48.992 --> 00:05:52.223
Then please allow us
to escort you to the palace.

00:05:52.295 --> 00:05:54.696
Wow... I'd heard
you knew King Kashue...

00:05:54.764 --> 00:05:57.631
...but I didn't think
you were this famous.

00:05:57.701 --> 00:06:00.636
Well, I didn't think a man
| could put my faith in...

00:06:00.704 --> 00:06:02.672
...would just be an
ordinary fighter.

00:06:03.707 --> 00:06:07.166
Open the gates!
Open the gates!

00:06:09.746 --> 00:06:11.111
That's Sir Parn!

00:06:11.181 --> 00:06:14.242
The hero who saved Flaim!

00:06:19.456 --> 00:06:22.482
The doorway to the audience chamber
is just ahead. Please wait a moment.

00:06:22.559 --> 00:06:25.824
All right.
And thanks for the escort.

00:06:30.533 --> 00:06:33.468
Looks like Flaim's
young knight corps.

00:06:33.536 --> 00:06:36.403
Candidates for
future knights of Flaim, huh?

00:06:38.575 --> 00:06:40.976
Come on, what's wrong?

00:06:43.546 --> 00:06:45.412
| win, Spark.

00:06:48.852 --> 00:06:50.377
Not yet!

00:06:50.987 --> 00:06:52.853
He's in pretty good shape.

00:06:52.923 --> 00:06:56.052
And he has a clear look to his eyes.

00:06:56.126 --> 00:06:59.027
I'd almost say he's
like how Parn used to be.

00:06:59.095 --> 00:07:01.564
You don't say.

00:07:16.479 --> 00:07:18.709
| think we can dispense
with the formalities.

00:07:18.782 --> 00:07:21.274
To me, you'll always
just be my good friends.

00:07:22.652 --> 00:07:25.781
Forgive our not staying
in touch, King Kashue.

00:07:25.855 --> 00:07:27.516
So, he is Kashue...

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.150
The mercenary king the
rumors speak so well of.

00:07:30.226 --> 00:07:32.160
You're looking well, Parn.

00:07:32.228 --> 00:07:34.492
As are you, Your Highness.

00:07:34.564 --> 00:07:36.931
| see three new faces
among your party now.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.798
Two appear to be mercenaries...

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:41.030
What's wrong?
Is trouble brewing again?

00:07:41.104 --> 00:07:43.937
Yes, sir. Actually, we came to
ask a favor of you, Highness.

00:07:45.275 --> 00:07:47.767
| see.
So, that's what's going on.

00:07:47.844 --> 00:07:51.405
Still, your story
is most serendipitous.

00:07:51.481 --> 00:07:53.108
What do you mean, Highness?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.881
The truth is that we
were just preparing...

00:07:56.953 --> 00:07:59.945
...to set out to slay the
fire dragon Shooting Star.

00:08:00.657 --> 00:08:03.991
The ancient dragon who
lives in Fire Dragon Mountain?!

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.963
Yes. Lately, Shooting Star
has begun to grow restless.

00:08:08.031 --> 00:08:12.525
It seems he's now flying into
western Flaim in search of prey.

00:08:14.237 --> 00:08:16.171
The grassy plains
of western Flaim...

00:08:16.239 --> 00:08:19.504
...are known as the fire
dragon's feeding grounds.

00:08:19.576 --> 00:08:21.840
Because that is
where the dragon feeds...

00:08:21.911 --> 00:08:25.438
...no one has claimed
the land for a long time.

00:08:25.515 --> 00:08:30.009
However, with all the
refugees coming into Blade...

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.021
...we've developed
a severe food shortage.

00:08:33.089 --> 00:08:35.888
To solve both the food
and refugee problems...

00:08:36.693 --> 00:08:38.627
...I took the risk
of establishing...

00:08:38.695 --> 00:08:40.857
...a village in the
dragon's feeding ground.

00:08:41.364 --> 00:08:43.025
However...

00:08:44.401 --> 00:08:47.393
The village was burned to the ground
in Shooting Star's attack...

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:51.930
...and not a soldier nor a
single villager was left alive.

00:08:53.877 --> 00:08:56.642
That's... That's terrible!

00:08:56.713 --> 00:08:59.182
The fault lies in
my own naive thinking.

00:08:59.249 --> 00:09:03.880
But to save my people, we must
be able to use that land!

00:09:03.953 --> 00:09:09.221
Quite. For a mostly desert kingdom
like Flaim, arable land is vital.

00:09:09.292 --> 00:09:11.989
And as Flaim's king,
| cannot forgive that...

00:09:12.062 --> 00:09:14.156
dragon for destroying that village.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:17.996
That's why we're preparing
to set out and fight it.

00:09:18.068 --> 00:09:22.301
In that case, we'd be happy
to lend our assistance! Right?

00:09:22.372 --> 00:09:26.502
But, Parn, what about Abram
on Blue Dragon Island?

00:09:26.576 --> 00:09:28.101
What do you...?

00:09:28.178 --> 00:09:32.081
The remaining ancient dragons
are Shooting Star and Abram.

00:09:32.148 --> 00:09:36.346
We don't know which one may
have the Scepter of Domination.

00:09:36.419 --> 00:09:41.755
If Abram has the scepter, while
we're of f killing Shooting Star...

00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:47.397
...and then Ashram kills Abram and
gains the scepter, it's all over.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.860
Then what should we do?

00:09:49.933 --> 00:09:52.868
It's simple.
We dispatch forces to both...

00:09:52.936 --> 00:09:56.304
...the fire dragon's feeding ground
and to Blue Dragon Island.

00:09:56.372 --> 00:09:59.000
But, while I could
split my forces...

00:09:59.075 --> 00:10:02.010
...I haven't the numbers
to do so effectively.

00:10:02.078 --> 00:10:05.275
And there'd be no way
we could defend Flaim.

00:10:05.348 --> 00:10:07.146
You won't have to do that.

00:10:07.217 --> 00:10:10.448
Ashram isn't dragging a whole
army around with him, right?

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:13.683
So what you should do is send
a small number of select troops.

00:10:13.756 --> 00:10:16.248
The important thing is quality,
not quantity, right?

00:10:18.428 --> 00:10:19.896
Quality, not quantity...

00:10:19.963 --> 00:10:24.059
You may oversimplify things,
but you do have a point.

00:10:24.134 --> 00:10:28.037
In that case, leave Abram
to us, Your Highness.

00:10:29.139 --> 00:10:30.072
Slayn!

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:35.044
You weren't counting on us to go
after Shooting Star with you.

00:10:35.111 --> 00:10:38.877
Knowing that,
| think we should go. Parn...

00:10:38.948 --> 00:10:41.940
Please take
Deed and help His Highness.

00:10:42.018 --> 00:10:45.318
You won't need a magic user
for this task. In addition...

00:10:45.388 --> 00:10:49.291
...I'd like Orson to lead the party
going to Blue Dragon Island.

00:10:50.827 --> 00:10:51.623
Orson?!

00:10:58.668 --> 00:11:00.796
This is terrible...

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:06.434
It seems the rumors of Shooting
Star's restlessness are true.

00:11:09.746 --> 00:11:14.240
80, this is the power
of the enemy we must fight...

00:11:15.985 --> 00:11:18.647
What's wrong, Priest Hobb?
Nervous?

00:11:18.721 --> 00:11:23.249
No. I have faith
in Myrii, the God of War.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:28.955
Just what I want to hear. I have
great hopes for you, Priest.

00:11:55.024 --> 00:11:57.083
Make Orson the leader?!

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:01.258
Yes. I've been thinking about this
a lot while we were traveling.

00:12:01.331 --> 00:12:05.063
About whether we can free
you from the spirit of anger.

00:12:05.134 --> 00:12:08.434
About how to protect against
your becoming a berserker.

00:12:08.504 --> 00:12:11.235
But the answer was there
right in front of me.

00:12:11.307 --> 00:12:14.106
- Parn, it was you.
- Me?

00:12:14.177 --> 00:12:18.910
<i>N all our travels, you've
experienced many different things.</i>

00:12:18.982 --> 00:12:22.680
As our leader, out of all the
rest of us in the party...

00:12:22.752 --> 00:12:26.052
...you learned to control the strong
feelings you carried inside of you.

00:12:26.122 --> 00:12:30.286
I get it! If he can learn to control
the strong feelings inside of him...

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.523
...then he'll be released
from the spirit of anger!

00:12:33.596 --> 00:12:36.657
Besides that, he's calm to
begin with, not emotional...

00:12:36.733 --> 00:12:40.169
...50 he should have little trouble
making decisions as a leader.

00:12:40.236 --> 00:12:42.500
Well, I guess you can't
call me calm, can you?

00:12:42.572 --> 00:12:46.167
Wait. I don't have what
it takes to be a leader.

00:12:46.242 --> 00:12:48.802
Besides, if |
become a berserker again...

00:12:48.878 --> 00:12:51.506
...I can't guarantee I won't
hurt someone on our side.

00:12:51.581 --> 00:12:52.776
Orson...

00:12:52.849 --> 00:12:56.683
I believe in the
strength of your will.

00:12:57.553 --> 00:13:00.215
If you think like
a leader, act like one...

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:04.158
...the result will be that you'll
feel like one in your heart.

00:13:04.227 --> 00:13:08.664
And then I'm sure the normal feelings
within you will awaken again.

00:13:08.731 --> 00:13:10.790
It's a great idea!
Let's try it!

00:13:10.867 --> 00:13:14.462
If it works, you won't
become a berserker anymore.

00:13:20.877 --> 00:13:23.437
What are you thinking
about that's so upsetting?

00:13:23.513 --> 00:13:25.914
Hm? Oh, thanks.

00:13:25.982 --> 00:13:27.950
Parn!

00:13:30.219 --> 00:13:31.209
Shirts!

00:13:31.287 --> 00:13:32.846
So, does it suit me?

00:13:32.922 --> 00:13:35.550
I hardly ever go to parties,
so I decided to wear a dress.

00:13:35.625 --> 00:13:37.354
Y- Yeah.
It looks really nice on you.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.521
Heh, thanks.
80, you wanna dance with me?

00:13:40.596 --> 00:13:42.394
N- No, thanks.
I'm a terrible dancer...

00:13:42.465 --> 00:13:44.399
Who cares how bad you are!

00:13:44.467 --> 00:13:45.298
Wha...? Parn!

00:13:45.368 --> 00:13:46.802
C'mon! C'mon!

00:13:51.607 --> 00:13:53.666
Thanks.

00:13:55.545 --> 00:13:59.140
Don't you mind?
Aren't you Parn's girlfriend?

00:13:59.215 --> 00:14:03.345
| wonder about that. He's a human
and I'm an elf, after all.

00:14:03.419 --> 00:14:07.322
Still, Shirts seems
to really like Parn.

00:14:07.657 --> 00:14:10.319
And how do you
feel about her, Orson?

00:14:10.393 --> 00:14:13.954
I don't know. I have no feelings.

00:14:14.297 --> 00:14:16.925
I haven't experienced
love since I was a child.

00:14:16.999 --> 00:14:19.263
I see... Don't worry, though.

00:14:19.335 --> 00:14:21.895
I'm sure this journey will
get your old feelings back.

00:14:21.971 --> 00:14:26.135
I hope so. Otherwise, making me the
leader will have been meaningless.

00:14:27.377 --> 00:14:29.004
Come on, Parn. Like this!

00:14:29.479 --> 00:14:31.743
There we go.

00:14:31.814 --> 00:14:34.215
Hey, why don't you
watch where you're going?!

00:14:34.283 --> 00:14:37.218
King Kashue!
Forgive me, Your Highness!

00:14:37.286 --> 00:14:41.223
Don't worry about it. Your name's
Shirts, isn't it? The new member.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:44.624
Thank you very much, Highness.

00:14:44.794 --> 00:14:47.525
So, are you
enjoying yourself, Parn?

00:14:47.597 --> 00:14:49.395
Hm? W- Well...

00:14:49.465 --> 00:14:51.593
Honest as ever.

00:14:51.667 --> 00:14:54.967
Do you think it isn't right to raise
the morale of the dragon fighters...

00:14:55.037 --> 00:14:58.564
...while other
people are going hungry?

00:14:58.641 --> 00:15:00.109
No, it's not that...

00:15:00.176 --> 00:15:03.976
However, sharing his people's
suffering is NOT the king's duty.

00:15:04.046 --> 00:15:07.243
Rather, his duty
is to save his people from it.

00:15:07.316 --> 00:15:08.613
| agree.

00:15:08.684 --> 00:15:10.778
As long as Shooting Star lives...

00:15:10.853 --> 00:15:14.448
...there's no saving the refugees
or the citizens of Flaim.

00:15:14.524 --> 00:15:17.050
And there's Ashram's ambitions.

00:15:17.126 --> 00:15:18.389
Excuse me, Your Highness...

00:15:18.461 --> 00:15:22.455
Hm? Oh, yes!
Parn, let me introduce you.

00:15:22.665 --> 00:15:23.325
Huh?

00:15:23.399 --> 00:15:24.958
| saw you this afternoon.

00:15:25.034 --> 00:15:28.026
This is Spark.
He shows a lot of promise.

00:15:28.104 --> 00:15:31.836
In exchange for serving me, I'm
letting him study various things.

00:15:31.908 --> 00:15:35.344
I'm Spark! It's really an honor
to meet you, Sir Parn!

00:15:35.411 --> 00:15:39.211
It's, well... It's my dream
to be a knight like you!

00:15:39.282 --> 00:15:40.681
Like me?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.548
Spark isn't the only
one who feels that way.

00:15:42.618 --> 00:15:48.022
You're the ideal of every child in
Flaim who wants to be a knight.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.821
I'M their ideal...?

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.725
Thank you, Spark.
I'm sure you can do it.

00:15:53.796 --> 00:15:56.458
Try to become a
better knight than I am.

00:15:58.167 --> 00:15:59.225
Come on, Parn, let's dan--

00:15:59.502 --> 00:16:03.996
How about it, Parn? Want to spar
a little, like we used to?

00:16:04.874 --> 00:16:06.433
Sure! It'd be my pleasure!

00:16:09.078 --> 00:16:11.103
Oh...! What's the big idea?!

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:14.673
| was the one
who just stole HIM!

00:16:18.821 --> 00:16:21.756
And what's your problem? I know
you don't have any feelings...

00:16:21.824 --> 00:16:25.192
...but could you at least say
"You look nice" or something?!

00:16:25.261 --> 00:16:26.353
You look nice.

00:16:26.429 --> 00:16:28.488
Right, right. Thanks SO much.

00:16:39.442 --> 00:16:40.409
Wow!

00:16:47.116 --> 00:16:49.175
Here he comes!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.389
Hm! You parried it!

00:16:58.561 --> 00:17:01.496
He's fantastic!
As to be expected of King Kashue!

00:17:01.564 --> 00:17:03.896
What do I do? What do I do?

00:17:03.966 --> 00:17:05.456
What's wrong? Finished already?

00:17:14.076 --> 00:17:15.703
You got me.

00:17:15.778 --> 00:17:17.712
That charge you
made was very good.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:20.078
However,
you still get distracted.

00:17:20.149 --> 00:17:22.481
If you'd charged in
after parrying my attack...

00:17:22.552 --> 00:17:24.281
...without thinking
about the consequences...

00:17:24.353 --> 00:17:26.344
...you may well have won.

00:17:26.422 --> 00:17:28.789
Y- Yes, sir.

00:17:30.126 --> 00:17:32.356
Thank you.

00:17:33.496 --> 00:17:35.692
Tell me, Parn.

00:17:35.765 --> 00:17:38.598
How would you
like to be a king?

00:17:38.668 --> 00:17:41.137
A..king, sir?

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.030
I hear what's
been going on in Alania.

00:17:44.106 --> 00:17:46.734
Several villages in the north have
declared their independence and...

00:17:46.809 --> 00:17:50.768
...a certain hero's been causing
trouble for Duke Raster in Alan, right?

00:17:50.846 --> 00:17:52.314
Right, a "hero"...

00:17:52.381 --> 00:17:54.748
I haven't been doing it alone.

00:17:54.817 --> 00:17:57.912
| owe a lot to Slayn and
the rest of the people of Zaxon.

00:17:57.987 --> 00:18:00.046
But people seek out heroes,

00:18:00.122 --> 00:18:03.285
especially in a war torn
world like this.

00:18:03.359 --> 00:18:07.956
I'd like to see you become
king and take over Alania.

00:18:08.297 --> 00:18:11.392
I think the people of
Alania would like that, too.

00:18:11.467 --> 00:18:15.097
But I don't think
| deserve to be a king.

00:18:15.171 --> 00:18:17.902
Oh, please. A king is just
a face for his kingdom.

00:18:17.974 --> 00:18:20.773
Besides,
you have excellent friends.

00:18:20.843 --> 00:18:22.777
If you ever need advice,
you could just ask them.

00:18:22.845 --> 00:18:24.006
But...

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.744
Have you heard that
there's a new king in Valis?

00:18:27.817 --> 00:18:31.310
We've heard that in Alania as well,
but I haven't heard who he is.

00:18:31.821 --> 00:18:34.722
Then I'll tell you.
Don't be too shocked, though.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:39.057
The new king of Valis is your
best friend, High Priest Etoh.

00:18:39.128 --> 00:18:42.223
Huh? Etoh?! You mean MY Etoh?!

00:18:42.298 --> 00:18:45.734
Yes, and whatever he can do,
| imagine you can do as well.

00:18:45.801 --> 00:18:48.361
Besides, if you're a man, you dream
of being a king at some point.

00:18:48.437 --> 00:18:51.839
This is a great chance for you.

00:18:52.408 --> 00:18:54.502
Please, let me have time
to think about this...

00:18:54.577 --> 00:18:58.241
Of course. Save your decision for
after this trouble is behind us.

00:18:58.314 --> 00:19:00.282
And if you feel you want to...

00:19:00.349 --> 00:19:03.785
...then Flaim will stand by
you with all its support.

00:19:05.187 --> 00:19:08.680
And besides that,
if you become a king...

00:19:08.758 --> 00:19:11.591
...then I can finally
treat you as my equal.

00:19:11.661 --> 00:19:14.528
And nothing would
make me happier than that.

00:19:21.003 --> 00:19:23.267
I have to concentrate now!

00:19:23.339 --> 00:19:28.470
<i>On killing the dragon and smashing
Ashram's ambitions for Marmo!</i>

00:19:28.544 --> 00:19:31.946
For the sake of Lodoss's future!

00:19:42.458 --> 00:19:43.687
Welcome...

00:19:43.759 --> 00:19:45.249
...to Lodoss Island!

00:19:45.327 --> 00:19:46.795
And now, what you've
been waiting for...

00:19:46.862 --> 00:19:48.523
...the next part of the show!

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:57.433
What's keeping King Kashue?

00:20:00.076 --> 00:20:03.876
Say, the king's a
master swordsman, isn't he?

00:20:03.946 --> 00:20:07.644
Yeah. He really kicked
Parn's butt 3 years ago.

00:20:10.486 --> 00:20:12.352
Ow! ow!

00:20:12.421 --> 00:20:15.288
All right, let's go!

00:20:17.359 --> 00:20:18.383
Okay, there it is!

00:20:23.299 --> 00:20:24.733
What's a knight when he sleeps?

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.269
A Good Knight!

00:20:31.107 --> 00:20:32.302
How's a SHIILDO (shield)
like being exhausted?

00:20:32.374 --> 00:20:35.207
AH, SHINDO! (I'm tired)!

00:20:38.147 --> 00:20:39.979
What's a dragon do sports on?

00:20:40.049 --> 00:20:41.107
Uh? Uh? Uh?

00:20:54.764 --> 00:20:56.391
A drampoline?

00:20:56.465 --> 00:20:58.593
Don't answer a
pun with a question!

00:21:03.572 --> 00:21:05.870
What kind of specialty is THAT?

00:21:05.941 --> 00:21:07.932
I've got it! I've got it!

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:09.569
What is it, Parn?

00:21:09.645 --> 00:21:13.275
The king's opening line will be him
getting into his armor and saying...

00:21:13.349 --> 00:21:18.685
"I am Kashue. Isn't my KATCHU
(armor) nice?" That's gotta be it!

00:21:20.156 --> 00:21:23.126
Oh, Parn, come on!

00:21:23.192 --> 00:21:25.058
Please! The guy's a king!

00:21:25.127 --> 00:21:28.222
He wouldn't appear using
a stupid joke like THAT!

00:21:28.297 --> 00:21:31.096
I... I guess not...

00:21:31.233 --> 00:21:32.758
You've grown in skill, Parn...

00:21:32.835 --> 00:21:34.860
I.. I couldn't
be happier than I am now!

00:22:59.455 --> 00:23:01.116
The free city of Raiden.

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:05.127
The port which leads to Blue Dragon
Island, where Abram dwells.

00:23:05.194 --> 00:23:08.027
But with the people of the
city living in fear of pirates...

00:23:08.097 --> 00:23:10.361
...no one dares go out onto the sea.

00:23:10.432 --> 00:23:14.300
What will Orson's decision
as leader be?

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:17.965
Next time, on Record of Lodoss War -
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:21.169
"Pirates...
The Ship of Dark Ambition".
